From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx7-media-csi: hold a CPU latency QoS request while
 streaming

imx7_csi_irq_handler() relies on the CSI bridge asserting
BIT_STATFF_INT alongside every frame-done interrupt to confirm its
internal base-address-switch bookkeeping is still in sync:

  if (!(status & BIT_STATFF_INT)) {
	  dev_warn(csi->dev, "Stat fifo is not full\n");
	  imx7_csi_error_recovery(csi);
	  csi->frame_skip++;
  }
  ...
  if (csi->frame_skip) {
	  dev_warn(csi->dev, "skip frame: %d\n", csi->frame_skip);
	  csi->frame_skip--;
	  goto out;
  }

When that status bit is missed, the driver does a full capture
pipeline reset (disable, clear the Rx FIFO, reflash the DMA
controller, re-enable) and drops the next captured frame outright.
This has been observed to fire repeatedly while a Wayland compositor
is actively driving the GPU, producing a stream of "Stat fifo is not
full" / "skip frame: N" warnings and visibly corrupted/shifted frames,
without any change in the CSI bridge or interrupt handler code itself.

The CSI bridge only gives a narrow window to sample this status before
the next frame overwrites it. Entering a deep CPU idle state between
interrupts adds enough wake-up latency to occasionally miss that
window, and this class of hardware needs a bounded interrupt handling
latency while actively capturing. Other V4L2 capture drivers with the
same requirement already solve this with a CPU latency QoS request
held for the duration of streaming, e.g. drivers/media/platform/via/
via-camera.c:

  /*
   * Enable clocks and set up the controller registers ... This is
   * the point where the controller goes into full active mode ...
   * we need a bounded interrupt latency to keep the FIFOs from
   * overrunning ... keep the CPU out of the deeper sleep states.
   */
  cpu_latency_qos_add_request(&cam->qos_request, 50);

Do the same here: acquire a 50us CPU latency QoS request in
imx7_csi_video_start_streaming() and release it in
imx7_csi_video_stop_streaming() (and on the streaming start error
path), so the CSI bridge's status FIFO is reliably sampled in time
regardless of what else is keeping the system busy.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate NXP proprietary driver
---
 drivers/media/platform/nxp/imx7-media-csi.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/imx7-media-csi.c b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/imx7-media-csi.c
index b15e841509f3..5e03280900a4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/imx7-media-csi.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/imx7-media-csi.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_qos.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
@@ -269,6 +270,16 @@ struct imx7_csi {
 	bool last_eof;
 	struct completion last_eof_completion;
 
+	/*
+	 * The CSI bridge reports frame completion through a status FIFO that
+	 * must be sampled within a tight window of the frame-done interrupt
+	 * (see imx7_csi_irq_handler()). Deep CPU idle states add enough
+	 * interrupt handling latency to miss that window, causing spurious
+	 * capture pipeline resets and dropped frames. Keep the CPU out of
+	 * deep idle states while actively streaming.
+	 */
+	struct pm_qos_request qos_request;
+
 	enum imx_csi_model model;
 };
 
@@ -1456,6 +1467,8 @@ static int imx7_csi_video_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq,
 		goto err_buffers;
 	}
 
+	cpu_latency_qos_add_request(&csi->qos_request, 50);
+
 	mutex_lock(&csi->mdev.graph_mutex);
 
 	ret = __video_device_pipeline_start(csi->vdev, &csi->pipe);
@@ -1474,6 +1487,7 @@ static int imx7_csi_video_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq,
 	__video_device_pipeline_stop(csi->vdev);
 err_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&csi->mdev.graph_mutex);
+	cpu_latency_qos_remove_request(&csi->qos_request);
 	dev_err(csi->dev, "pipeline start failed with %d\n", ret);
 err_buffers:
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&csi->q_lock, flags);
@@ -1497,6 +1511,8 @@ static void imx7_csi_video_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq)
 	__video_device_pipeline_stop(csi->vdev);
 	mutex_unlock(&csi->mdev.graph_mutex);
 
+	cpu_latency_qos_remove_request(&csi->qos_request);
+
 	/* release all active buffers */
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&csi->q_lock, flags);
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(frame, tmp, &csi->ready_q, list) {
-- 
2.54.0
